.TH PKSTAT 1 "2026-08-30" "SPS 1.0" "SPS Commands"
.SH NAME
pkstat \- inspect locally installed SPS package state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
pkstat [PACKAGE]
pkstat --files PACKAGE
pkstat --owns PATH
pkstat --explicit
pkstat --orphans
pkstat --size PACKAGE
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkstat
answers installed-state queries entirely from local metadata. It does not
refresh repositories or access the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --files " package"
List the package manifest.
.TP
.BI --owns " path"
Print the package owning a non-directory payload path.
.TP
.B --explicit
List the explicit world set.
.TP
.B --orphans
List dependency-installed packages unreachable from every explicit world root
through installed runtime dependency records. This is graph reachability, so
entire abandoned dependency chains are reported.
.TP
.BI --size " package"
Print the current byte size of regular files in the package manifest.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 for usage, 3 for missing package/owner, 8 for
unreadable filesystem state, and 11 for malformed/unavailable database state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkcheck (1),
.BR pkmark (1),
.BR pkin (1),
.BR pkdel (1)
